# Ruinas del Origen (D1, contract 68: Chapter 10), 13 x 14, a cave-like ruin (no bike) behind the sealed gate of the Meseta Cumbre. column = i, row = j. The way in is the door mat (7,13) <- Meseta Cumbre ((4,0) behind the sealed slab);
# the hero arrives at (7,12) facing N. Look: the user's approved RUINAS scenes (tools/c10_mock.py): BIG light ancient slabs (2 x 2, `aslab_<i%2><j%2>`), EIGHT pedestals in a ring (they light up), the mural stele of Genesa and Arkegen
# on the back wall, fallen columns. THE PUZZLE: the mural (7,2) tells the order in which the eight symbols were born (LUZ, MAR, TIERRA, FUEGO, VIENTO, VIDA, NOCHE, ECO); each pedestal is carved with one symbol (talking to it asks
# "place a fragment?"); a correct pedestal lights (flags lit_1 .. lit_7, the 8th is ruins_solved), a wrong one puts every stone out again (the fragments are never consumed). The 8th correct stone sets ruins_solved: GENESA appears
# at the ring's centre (7,7). ONE CHANCE: she asks YES / NO, the flag genesa_try is set BEFORE the battle (a faint or a flight cannot undo it), the legendary fight (`wild_set genesa 50 + 128`); afterwards genesa_gone hides her
# for good. A save that already holds Genesa (the old Lin gift, flag genesa_given) gets the shrine without a battle (ruins_enter sets genesa_gone; `solved` hands a consolation).
@map ruinas_origen
@size 13 14
@interior no
@cave yes
@area ruinas_origen
@bg 0
@fill aslab_00
@spawn in 7 12 N
@legend
  a  tile=aslab_00
  b  tile=aslab_10
  c  tile=aslab_01
  d  tile=aslab_11
  K  tile=none object=wall_corner
  w  tile=none object=wall_j
  |  tile=none object=wall_i
  M  tile=aslab_10 object=ostele interact=look script=mural
  e  tile=aslab_11 object=fcol_i
  g  tile=aslab_00 object=fcol_j
  G  tile=aslab_11 npc=genesa_ow id=genesa face=S solid=yes script=genesa_talk show_flag=ruins_solved hide_flag=genesa_gone
  m  tile=mat
  1  tile=aslab_10 object=ped0 interact=look script=ped_luz npc=ped_lit id=p1 face=S show_flag=lit_1
  2  tile=aslab_01 object=ped0 interact=look script=ped_mar npc=ped_lit id=p2 face=S show_flag=lit_2
  3  tile=aslab_01 object=ped0 interact=look script=ped_tierra npc=ped_lit id=p3 face=S show_flag=lit_3
  4  tile=aslab_10 object=ped0 interact=look script=ped_fuego npc=ped_lit id=p4 face=S show_flag=lit_4
  5  tile=aslab_10 object=ped0 interact=look script=ped_viento npc=ped_lit id=p5 face=S show_flag=lit_5
  6  tile=aslab_01 object=ped0 interact=look script=ped_vida npc=ped_lit id=p6 face=S show_flag=lit_6
  7  tile=aslab_10 object=ped0 interact=look script=ped_noche npc=ped_lit id=p7 face=S show_flag=lit_7
  8  tile=aslab_01 object=ped0 interact=look script=ped_eco npc=ped_lit id=p8 face=S show_flag=ruins_solved
@grid
  Kwwwwwwwwwwww
  |dcdcdcdcdcdc
  |bababaMababa
  |dcecdcdcdcdc
  |babababababg
  |dcdcd3d6dcdc
  |baba5aba1aba
  |dcdcdcGcdcdc
  |baba7aba4aba
  |dcdcd2d8dcec
  |bgbababababa
  |dcdcdcdcdcdc
  |babababababa
  |dcdcdcmcdcdc
@warp m -> meseta_cumbre spawn=ruins_door

# The door of the ruins: a save that already holds Genesa (the old Lin gift) or that spent its one chance has no Genesa here (she is hidden at once: the map's NPC state is read from the flags).
@script ruins_enter on_enter
    jf genesa_try gone
    jf genesa_given gone
    end
  gone:
    setf genesa_gone
@end

# The mural: five pages that tell the order of the eight symbols (the pedestals' carvings); once the puzzle is solved the last words of the legend follow.
@script mural interact
    say ru.mural.1
    say ru.mural.2
    say ru.mural.3
    say ru.mural.4
    say ru.mural.5
    jnf ruins_solved done
    say ru.mural.end1
    say ru.mural.end2
  done:
    end
@end

# Wrong order (or a stone out of turn): every light goes out again; the fragments stay in the bag.
@script reset called
    clrf lit_1
    clrf lit_2
    clrf lit_3
    clrf lit_4
    clrf lit_5
    clrf lit_6
    clrf lit_7
    sfx cancel
@end

@script ped_luz called
    jf lit_1 done
    ask ru.p.luz
    jv 0 1 yes
    end
  yes:
    setf lit_1
    sfx item
    say ru.placed
    end
  done:
    say ru.lit
@end

@script ped_mar called
    jf lit_2 done
    ask ru.p.mar
    jv 0 1 yes
    end
  yes:
    jnf lit_1 wrong
    setf lit_2
    sfx item
    say ru.placed
    end
  wrong:
    call reset
    say ru.wrong
    end
  done:
    say ru.lit
@end

@script ped_tierra called
    jf lit_3 done
    ask ru.p.tierra
    jv 0 1 yes
    end
  yes:
    jnf lit_2 wrong
    setf lit_3
    sfx item
    say ru.placed
    end
  wrong:
    call reset
    say ru.wrong
    end
  done:
    say ru.lit
@end

@script ped_fuego called
    jf lit_4 done
    ask ru.p.fuego
    jv 0 1 yes
    end
  yes:
    jnf lit_3 wrong
    setf lit_4
    sfx item
    say ru.placed
    end
  wrong:
    call reset
    say ru.wrong
    end
  done:
    say ru.lit
@end

@script ped_viento called
    jf lit_5 done
    ask ru.p.viento
    jv 0 1 yes
    end
  yes:
    jnf lit_4 wrong
    setf lit_5
    sfx item
    say ru.placed
    end
  wrong:
    call reset
    say ru.wrong
    end
  done:
    say ru.lit
@end

@script ped_vida called
    jf lit_6 done
    ask ru.p.vida
    jv 0 1 yes
    end
  yes:
    jnf lit_5 wrong
    setf lit_6
    sfx item
    say ru.placed
    end
  wrong:
    call reset
    say ru.wrong
    end
  done:
    say ru.lit
@end

@script ped_noche called
    jf lit_7 done
    ask ru.p.noche
    jv 0 1 yes
    end
  yes:
    jnf lit_6 wrong
    setf lit_7
    sfx item
    say ru.placed
    end
  wrong:
    call reset
    say ru.wrong
    end
  done:
    say ru.lit
@end

@script ped_eco called
    jf ruins_solved done
    ask ru.p.eco
    jv 0 1 yes
    end
  yes:
    jnf lit_7 wrong
    call solved
    end
  wrong:
    call reset
    say ru.wrong
    end
  done:
    say ru.lit
@end

# The eighth stone: the whole ring shines and Genesa appears at its centre (her NPC's show flag is ruins_solved). A save that already holds Genesa gets the shrine without a second battle and a consolation (5 Growth Seeds).
@script solved called
    setf ruins_solved
    sfx evo_done
    say ru.solved
    jnf genesa_given appear
    say ru.old1
    give_item growth_seed 5
    jv 0 0 old_full
    say gl.d1.candies
    say ru.old2
    end
  old_full:
    say gl.found.full
    end
  appear:
    sfx legend_cry
    say ru.appear
@end

# Genesa. ONE chance: `genesa_try` is committed before the battle and read by ruins_enter, so a faint (the blackout cuts the script), a flight (the result 2) or a win (the foe faints) all end with her gone; a catch ends it too.
# EXCEPT the result 4 (WILD_NOTOPEN, §72: the battle plugin / heap could not open, no fight took place): the chance is given back (`clrf genesa_try`), she stays and says the air trembles.
# The fight is the legendary idiom of contract 52 written by hand (`wild_set` with level + 128, the music, the intro and the cry follow). Genesa L50 (is L30; this is the post-game).
@script genesa_talk npc
    npc_face_hero genesa
    say ru.genesa.1
    say ru.genesa.2
    ask ru.genesa.ask
    jv 0 1 go
    say ru.genesa.wait
    end
  go:
    setf genesa_try
    sfx legend_cry
    wild_set genesa 178
    wild_go 0
    jv 0 4 noopen
    setf genesa_gone
    jv 0 3 caught
    say ru.genesa.gone
    end
  noopen:
    clrf genesa_try
    say ru.genesa.retry
    end
  caught:
    say ru.genesa.got
    say ru.mural.end2
@end
